WEBVTT

00:00:04.245 --> 00:00:05.899
GUY:
Ah.

00:00:06.073 --> 00:00:08.031
I can't believe they kept
these old picture albums.

00:00:08.205 --> 00:00:10.425
That's the Bettermans.

00:00:10.599 --> 00:00:12.775
Okay, this is my mom,
this is my dad,

00:00:12.949 --> 00:00:14.342
and that's me.

00:00:14.516 --> 00:00:15.691
[laughing]

00:00:15.865 --> 00:00:18.346
Yeah, I get it. I was skinny.

00:00:22.132 --> 00:00:25.266
[sighs] It's pretty great
here, huh, Belt?

00:00:26.963 --> 00:00:28.356
-[laughs]
-Shh.

00:00:30.619 --> 00:00:32.621
[Chunky grunts]

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:36.625
-DAWN: [grunts] Whoo.
-EEP: [grunts] Whee.

00:00:36.799 --> 00:00:37.844
[Chunky groans]

00:00:38.018 --> 00:00:39.323
[both shushing, chuckling]

00:00:39.498 --> 00:00:40.847
-[footsteps approaching]
-[Eep gasps]

00:00:42.239 --> 00:00:43.893
Is that my dad?

00:00:44.067 --> 00:00:46.069
-Hide me.
-Mr. Betterman?

00:00:47.027 --> 00:00:48.550
"Mr. Betterman"?

00:00:48.724 --> 00:00:50.421
[blows raspberry, laughs]
It's just Guy.

00:00:50.596 --> 00:00:53.337
-Hi, Guy!
-Hey, you.

00:00:53.512 --> 00:00:55.862
-Where'd you go?
-Took Chunky for a joyride.

00:00:56.036 --> 00:00:58.212
-Joyride!
-Joyride?

00:00:58.386 --> 00:00:59.692
We rolled the death...

00:00:59.866 --> 00:01:01.258
-Outside the wall.
-...cat. [hisses]

00:01:01.432 --> 00:01:03.957
You took Dawn for a joyride

00:01:04.131 --> 00:01:05.741
outside the wall?

00:01:05.915 --> 00:01:07.700
-Yeah. -Well, the Bettermans,
they-they don't want

00:01:07.874 --> 00:01:09.049
Dawn outside the wall.

00:01:09.223 --> 00:01:10.354
They built the wall
for a reason.

00:01:10.529 --> 00:01:12.313
You know, to keep everyone safe.

00:01:12.487 --> 00:01:14.271
-Guy, relax.
-Yeah, Guy.

00:01:14.445 --> 00:01:17.840
[in deep voice]:
Take it down low.

00:01:18.014 --> 00:01:19.233
What's wrong with her?

00:01:19.407 --> 00:01:21.061
Ah, it's just a reaction
to the bee venom.

00:01:21.235 --> 00:01:23.367
-Bee venom?
-Bee venom!

00:01:23.542 --> 00:01:25.326
-What the...!
-[pulsing]

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:27.502
-[scoffs] It's just
a little bee sting. -"Little"?

00:01:27.676 --> 00:01:30.636
Hey, you're not the boss of me.

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:32.289
-This is a very severe...
-DAWN: Shh.

00:01:32.463 --> 00:01:36.163
-[Eep chuckles] -Eep, this is
a very severe bee sting.

00:01:36.337 --> 00:01:38.382
-"This is a very severe
bee sting." -She's fine.

00:01:38.557 --> 00:01:39.775
No, no. She's-she's not fine.

00:01:39.949 --> 00:01:41.472
-I'm fine. [groans]
-Dawn.

00:01:41.647 --> 00:01:43.953
Eep, that was not smart.

00:01:44.127 --> 00:01:45.302
She could have been
seriously hurt.

00:01:45.476 --> 00:01:46.739
You got to think
about these things.

00:01:46.913 --> 00:01:48.958
Why are you acting like this?

00:01:49.132 --> 00:01:50.438
-You like adventures.
-GUY: No.

00:01:50.612 --> 00:01:52.179
No, I like not dying.

00:01:52.353 --> 00:01:53.528
Things are different now.

00:01:53.702 --> 00:01:55.530
But she needed to get out.

00:01:55.704 --> 00:01:58.489
She's just like me.
This is her cave.

00:01:58.664 --> 00:02:00.796
No, she's not like you.
This is not her cave.

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:02.668
She's not a cave girl.

00:02:04.278 --> 00:02:06.802
"Cave girl"?

00:02:11.111 --> 00:02:13.113
What does he mean
by "cave girl"?

00:02:13.287 --> 00:02:15.071
I'll give him a cave girl.

00:02:15.245 --> 00:02:17.073
[growls, hisses]

00:02:17.247 --> 00:02:19.249
[growling, chuckling]

00:02:23.079 --> 00:02:26.126
I trust you've all brought
your appetites.

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:28.041
Chef Hope's
been working hard all day.

00:02:28.215 --> 00:02:29.564
THUNK:
Mmm.

00:02:29.738 --> 00:02:31.566
This is so good,
Mrs. Better-mom.

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:34.525
You're eating
the flower arrangement.

00:02:36.963 --> 00:02:38.225
-Wow.
-[Dawn grunting]

00:02:38.399 --> 00:02:40.836
Uh, Grug, Ugga,
what can we offer you?

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:42.316
-Ah, we're good.
-Yeah.

00:02:42.490 --> 00:02:44.318
We ate a little something
on the way over.

00:02:44.492 --> 00:02:46.842
[burps]
Oops. Pardon me.

00:02:47.016 --> 00:02:49.323
Uh... okay.

00:02:49.497 --> 00:02:50.890
Oh, look!

00:02:51.064 --> 00:02:52.935
-Oh!
-Guy and Dawn are here...

00:02:53.109 --> 00:02:54.415
-[blows raspberry]
-...together.

00:02:54.589 --> 00:02:56.286
[Dawn chuckles]

00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:57.810
You good to do this?

00:02:57.984 --> 00:02:59.681
Just try to keep
your giant hand out of sight.

00:02:59.855 --> 00:03:01.465
-Got ya! [chuckles]
-[gasps]

00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:03.642
-[leaves rustling]
-[Eep grunting]

00:03:06.166 --> 00:03:08.255
Oh, welcome, Eep.
Your seat is over here,

00:03:08.429 --> 00:03:10.170
next to... Gran.

00:03:11.693 --> 00:03:14.435
We're not done.
You called me a cave girl.

00:03:14.609 --> 00:03:17.612
-But y-y-you are a cave girl.
-[blowing raspberry]

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:22.095
But you said "cave girl"
like it's a bad thing.

00:03:22.269 --> 00:03:25.185
What's wrong
with cave people, Guy?

00:03:25.359 --> 00:03:27.056
-There's nothing wrong
with cave people. -[clatters]

00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:28.797
Can I get you a towel
or a utensil or something?

00:03:28.971 --> 00:03:30.494
[gulping]

00:03:30.669 --> 00:03:32.453
-[burps] I'm good.
-[shatters]

00:03:32.627 --> 00:03:34.673
Why are you acting like this?

00:03:34.847 --> 00:03:36.413
I'm just acting
like a cave girl, Guy.

00:03:36.587 --> 00:03:38.589
But I guess that's not
good enough for you anymore.

00:03:38.764 --> 00:03:40.461
I never said that.

00:03:40.635 --> 00:03:42.506
Grug, let's take this moment
to talk about your great idea.

00:03:42.681 --> 00:03:44.421
-Uh, what?
-PHIL: Grug felt,

00:03:44.595 --> 00:03:46.423
and I concurred,
that Guy should be

00:03:46.597 --> 00:03:48.774
with his kind of people--
evolved people--

00:03:48.948 --> 00:03:51.211
and Eep should stay
with her kind.

00:03:51.385 --> 00:03:52.865
So we made a deal.

00:03:53.039 --> 00:03:55.302
-Say again?
-What deal? -His deal.

00:03:56.085 --> 00:03:58.218
-Your idea.
-Your idea?

00:03:58.392 --> 00:04:00.002
Guy stays with us,
and Eep stays with her pack.

00:04:00.176 --> 00:04:01.612
Grug's words, not mine.

00:04:01.787 --> 00:04:04.050
-You tried to get rid of me?
-Really, Dad?

00:04:04.224 --> 00:04:06.922
No. Honey, I don't think that.
I mean, he made me think

00:04:07.096 --> 00:04:09.403
that I thought that.
He tricked me!

00:04:09.577 --> 00:04:11.535
He took me into
his stupid secret man cave,

00:04:11.710 --> 00:04:14.060
-and he tricked me.
-What's a man cave?

00:04:14.234 --> 00:04:16.802
It's a place I go to get away.

00:04:16.976 --> 00:04:18.412
Away from what?

00:04:18.586 --> 00:04:21.458
-Away from you! Duh.
-What?!

00:04:21.632 --> 00:04:23.373
-We're all thinking it.
-How dare you.

00:04:23.547 --> 00:04:26.202
-How dare you!
-How dare the both of you!

00:04:26.376 --> 00:04:28.770
-[both gasp] -You're trying
to fix me up with Guy?

00:04:28.944 --> 00:04:31.599
-What happened to your hand?
-Oh! I got stung by a bee.

00:04:31.773 --> 00:04:33.862
Oh! Outside the wall.
[chuckles] Oh!

00:04:34.036 --> 00:04:36.343
-You went outside the wall?
-Outside the wall?

00:04:36.517 --> 00:04:38.562
-This is all your fault!
-Oh, our fault?

00:04:38.737 --> 00:04:40.390
-Can I say something?
-ALL: No!

00:04:40.564 --> 00:04:43.089
-Okay. -I can't believe
you actually made that deal.

00:04:43.263 --> 00:04:45.613
-What did they do to you?
-I got scars.

00:04:45.787 --> 00:04:46.919
Our baby!

00:04:47.093 --> 00:04:48.398
GRUG:
It was really hot.

00:04:48.572 --> 00:04:51.271
I was full of shark milk.
I was naked!

00:04:51.445 --> 00:04:52.315
HOPE:
Why, Phil?

00:04:52.489 --> 00:04:53.839
Why?!

00:04:54.013 --> 00:04:55.666
Because privacy
promotes individuality!

00:04:55.841 --> 00:04:57.190
Unofficial motto!

00:04:57.364 --> 00:04:59.192
Well, kiddo, looks like
we all have something to hide.

00:04:59.366 --> 00:05:01.237
-[hisses]
-[screams]

00:05:01.411 --> 00:05:03.805
-[overlapping shouting]
-Why is everybody yelling?

00:05:03.979 --> 00:05:05.024
That's it!

00:05:05.198 --> 00:05:06.634
Come on, Guy. We're leaving.

00:05:06.808 --> 00:05:08.070
Wait, hold on a second.

00:05:08.244 --> 00:05:09.419
First, you wanted
to get rid of me, Grug,

00:05:09.593 --> 00:05:11.160
and now you want me
to come with you?

00:05:11.334 --> 00:05:13.249
You were trying
to take my daughter away.

00:05:13.423 --> 00:05:14.598
Promising my baby girl
butterflies

00:05:14.773 --> 00:05:15.948
and babbling brooks.

00:05:16.122 --> 00:05:17.427
Aha!

00:05:17.601 --> 00:05:19.255
You see?
I knew you were listening.

00:05:19.429 --> 00:05:21.605
There is no privacy
with you people.

00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:23.303
Oh, you mean cave people?

00:05:23.477 --> 00:05:25.348
Not what I said.
Positives, Eep.

00:05:25.522 --> 00:05:28.612
That's all I'm saying.
Lots of things here are better.

00:05:28.787 --> 00:05:31.224
-"Better"?
-Like not starving.

00:05:31.398 --> 00:05:32.965
No sleep pile.

00:05:33.139 --> 00:05:34.401
What's wrong
with the sleep pile?

00:05:34.575 --> 00:05:37.317
Oh, come on, Eep!
The sleep pile reeks!

00:05:37.491 --> 00:05:38.840
Reeks of love!

00:05:39.014 --> 00:05:41.190
Well, at least I smell like me.
[sniffing]

00:05:41.364 --> 00:05:43.932
I don't even know
what you smell like.

00:05:44.106 --> 00:05:45.629
Flowers and soft rain.

00:05:45.804 --> 00:05:47.588
I don't even know
who you are anymore!

00:05:47.762 --> 00:05:50.547
With your vanilla
and your stupid neck rock!

00:05:50.721 --> 00:05:53.463
It's this place.
This place is...

00:05:53.637 --> 00:05:55.944
Home! This place is home!

00:05:56.118 --> 00:05:57.685
"Home"?

00:05:57.859 --> 00:05:59.905
This is the place
my parents wanted me to find.

00:06:00.079 --> 00:06:02.211
This is Tomorrow.

00:06:03.778 --> 00:06:07.521
Well, clearly, I don't belong
in this Tomorrow.

00:06:08.914 --> 00:06:10.959
I'm leaving.

00:06:11.133 --> 00:06:12.613
Are you coming with me?

00:06:13.919 --> 00:06:16.573
I, um... I can't.

00:06:20.273 --> 00:06:22.362
Then I guess we have
two different Tomorrows.

